<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.060 percent from 10.097 percent at the previous auction on December 23.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: July 1, 1997 (June 24, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.060 percent (10.097)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 800.550 million (909.475 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 949.325 million (1.179 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.997-10.087 percent (9.999-10.107)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.997-10.400 percent (9.999-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 60 (71)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 79 (103)</p>
<p>$= 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
